WEBVTT

00:06.715 --> 00:08.924
- [soldiers laughing]
- [soldier] Now, the thing

00:08.925 --> 00:10.801
about this one night,
and you guys know me.

00:10.802 --> 00:13.303
Like, I'm fuckin' easy
on voters, right?

00:13.304 --> 00:15.431
- That ain't what they say.
- Oh, yeah, well, fuck them

00:15.432 --> 00:17.433
because they'd rather
have me than Greenberg.

00:17.434 --> 00:20.352
- Oh, this is a Greenberg story.
- [laughter]

00:20.353 --> 00:21.979
So, I got three voters
against the wall.

00:21.980 --> 00:24.857
I caught 'em red-handed
disseminating pamphlets, right?

00:24.858 --> 00:27.109
- WLF stuff?
- I thought it was.

00:27.110 --> 00:28.861
Turned out later
it was some, like,
religious crap,

00:28.862 --> 00:30.362
but I didn't fuckin' know that.

00:30.363 --> 00:33.615
So, I call for backup.
Guess who shows up?

00:33.616 --> 00:35.784
- [soldiers] Greenberg!
- Greenberg!

00:35.785 --> 00:37.619
- [laughter]
- He pulls up,

00:37.620 --> 00:40.622
gets out of his truck.
He's in a fuckin' mood, okay?

00:40.623 --> 00:42.207
I can already tell,
and he's all like,

00:42.208 --> 00:43.876
"What are you
fuckin' calling for?

00:43.877 --> 00:45.669
"What, you can't handle
three voters?

00:45.670 --> 00:47.504
What did these
fuckin' pussies even do?"

00:47.505 --> 00:49.298
- [laughter]
- I say, "I caught them

00:49.299 --> 00:51.967
out here disseminating."

00:51.968 --> 00:55.721
And he goes, "What?
You fuckin' perverts

00:55.722 --> 00:59.058
are out here jerking off
and splooging on my streets?"

00:59.059 --> 01:01.393
- [laughter]
- Holy shit!

01:01.394 --> 01:04.188
I swear to God.
So, one of the voters turns back

01:04.189 --> 01:06.315
to look at me like,
"Are you gonna tell him?"

01:06.316 --> 01:08.317
I look back at him
like, "Fuck no."

01:08.318 --> 01:10.736
And that's when the guy decides
to open his mouth anyway

01:10.737 --> 01:14.990
and goes, "Well, actually,
the word 'disseminate' means..."

01:14.991 --> 01:16.492
- And boom!
- Oh!

01:16.493 --> 01:18.660
Greenberg slams
his fuckin' head
against the wall.

01:18.661 --> 01:22.081
There goes his teeth,
just blood fuckin' everywhere.

01:22.082 --> 01:25.000
And-- and Greenberg goes,

01:25.001 --> 01:28.003
"No one asked you, jizz boy!"

01:28.004 --> 01:30.006
[laughter]

01:37.931 --> 01:40.058
Wh-Why do you call them that?

01:44.062 --> 01:46.106
The citizens, why do
you call them voters?

01:47.107 --> 01:48.565
I don't know.

01:48.566 --> 01:50.734
'Cause that's what
we fucking call 'em.
Who cares?

01:50.735 --> 01:52.695
'Cause we took away
their rights.

01:56.741 --> 01:58.408
Took away their right to vote,
and somebody

01:58.409 --> 02:00.620
started calling them
voters to mock them.

02:03.998 --> 02:05.291
So, now you know.

02:10.505 --> 02:11.964
I didn't mean
anything by it, Sergeant.

02:11.965 --> 02:13.925
Of course, you didn't.
You're thoughtless.

02:15.176 --> 02:17.345
- [driver] Sarge.
- [brakes squealing]

02:20.849 --> 02:22.851
[engine idling]

02:23.893 --> 02:26.896
[♪ tense music playing]

02:32.861 --> 02:33.986
Keep it running.

02:33.987 --> 02:36.156
- [driver] Copy.
- How many?

02:36.906 --> 02:38.073
[Sergeant Isaac Dixon]
A lot.

02:38.074 --> 02:40.075
Could be WLF.
Lock and load.

02:40.076 --> 02:42.953
- [Isaac] No.
- Sarge.

02:42.954 --> 02:45.664
I'm gonna go talk to them.
Alone.

02:45.665 --> 02:47.291
- But protocol.
- Protocol is to obey

02:47.292 --> 02:49.293
your commanding officer.
Period. The end.

02:49.294 --> 02:51.128
Now, if we go
out there in force,

02:51.129 --> 02:53.089
this'll end up
the way it always does.

02:54.090 --> 02:55.633
'Cause you're all Greenberg.

03:00.430 --> 03:02.639
You wanna die?
Fine.

03:02.640 --> 03:05.685
[♪ tense music playing]

03:19.115 --> 03:20.200
You.

03:22.702 --> 03:24.078
Come with me.

03:26.206 --> 03:27.373
Learn something.

03:34.923 --> 03:38.343
[♪ tense music continues]

03:57.570 --> 03:58.821
You Isaac?

04:02.408 --> 04:03.952
You Hanrahan?

04:16.464 --> 04:18.091
[sighs]

04:26.975 --> 04:29.017
- [metal pins clinging]
- [grenades bouncing]

04:29.018 --> 04:30.560
[soldiers shouting]

04:30.561 --> 04:32.688
[muffled shouting continues]

04:32.689 --> 04:34.774
[explosions booming]

04:36.234 --> 04:38.319
[birds squawking]

04:40.363 --> 04:42.531
[driver gasping, wheezing]

04:42.532 --> 04:44.242
[gunfire]

04:54.460 --> 04:55.878
Welcome to the fight.

05:04.595 --> 05:06.388
Now, make your choice.

05:06.389 --> 05:09.309
♪

05:11.561 --> 05:14.564
[♪ pensive theme music playing]

06:12.580 --> 06:14.582
[♪ theme concludes]

06:18.836 --> 06:21.839
[rustling]

06:22.673 --> 06:24.675
[grunting]

06:39.649 --> 06:41.566
[Dina] [sighs]
No pain meds.

06:41.567 --> 06:43.111
[Ellie] Anything else?

06:44.153 --> 06:46.364
[Dina] Probably nothing
anyone wanted.

07:00.420 --> 07:03.171
Ooh! You rockin'
a yeast infection?

07:03.172 --> 07:05.883
[Ellie] Not today,
but gimme time.

07:10.263 --> 07:12.889
Good news.
I found a gallon jug of milk.

07:12.890 --> 07:14.182
Yum.

07:14.183 --> 07:17.562
Make sure to smell it first,
just in case.

07:19.021 --> 07:22.732
[Ellie] Alright, I give up.
I'm gonna stand watch outside.

07:22.733 --> 07:24.526
Yeah, I'm done.

07:24.527 --> 07:26.320
There's nothing else back h--

07:30.783 --> 07:34.369
Hey, I'm gonna pee.
Gimme a minute.

07:34.370 --> 07:35.538
[Ellie] Okay.

07:46.674 --> 07:49.677
[♪ gentle music playing]

07:52.513 --> 07:54.515
- [Shimmer snorts]
- [bird cawing]

08:02.315 --> 08:04.150
[Dina]
'Kay, good to go.

08:12.492 --> 08:13.576
Thanks.

08:15.119 --> 08:16.287
You okay?

08:17.497 --> 08:18.539
Yeah.

08:21.959 --> 08:23.044
[Dina grunts]

08:24.754 --> 08:27.006
Alright, hit it.
People to kill.

08:28.466 --> 08:29.925
Okay.

08:29.926 --> 08:32.511
- [clicking tongue]
- [Shimmer nickering]

08:32.512 --> 08:35.556
[♪ gentle music
continues playing]

08:38.434 --> 08:40.436
[Shimmer snorts]

08:41.020 --> 08:44.022
[Dina] I don't understand.
I thought they bombed here.

08:44.023 --> 08:47.026
Yeah, I heard that too.
Guess not this part.

08:53.824 --> 08:55.617
[Dina] What's up with
all the rainbows?

08:55.618 --> 08:56.660
[Ellie] I don't know.

08:56.661 --> 08:59.038
Maybe they
were all optimists.

08:59.956 --> 09:01.958
[birds squawking]

09:07.505 --> 09:09.507
[♪ ominous music playing]

09:10.091 --> 09:12.093
[insects buzzing]

09:13.636 --> 09:16.389
[Ellie]
So much for happy,
proud Rainbow Town.

09:22.228 --> 09:24.312
[Dina] I've never seen
a tank this close.

09:24.313 --> 09:25.898
Me neither.

09:27.608 --> 09:30.193
- Ellie. Ellie!
- Just cover me.

09:30.194 --> 09:32.238
I'm gonna check
if there's any ammo in there.

09:33.114 --> 09:35.116
[insects buzzing]

09:45.293 --> 09:46.836
[sighs]

09:47.503 --> 09:50.672
[Dina] Man, FEDRA got
fucked up out here.

09:50.673 --> 09:52.424
You think it was the WLF?

09:52.425 --> 09:54.259
I don't know.

09:54.260 --> 09:56.344
All these bodies
are in FEDRA gear.

09:56.345 --> 09:58.263
Almost looks like they
were fighting each other.

09:58.264 --> 10:00.516
Huh.
Good eye.

10:01.726 --> 10:03.144
I wonder what
that was about.

10:04.186 --> 10:05.395
[metal lid banging loudly]

10:05.396 --> 10:07.440
[birds squawking]

10:15.823 --> 10:17.742
[birds cawing]

10:21.329 --> 10:24.456
- Ooh.
- What is it?

10:24.457 --> 10:27.542
Three burnt skeletons.
Like Apollo 1.

10:27.543 --> 10:29.377
[Dina] What?

10:29.378 --> 10:32.881
Grissom, White, Chaffee.
Early astronauts.

10:32.882 --> 10:35.050
They were supposed to be
the first ones to go
to the moon,

10:35.051 --> 10:37.135
but they never made it
off the launchpad.

10:37.136 --> 10:38.679
Burned up in their capsule.

10:40.598 --> 10:44.726
Well, at least they died
for something worthwhile.

10:44.727 --> 10:46.227
Yeah. [sighs]

10:46.228 --> 10:48.856
These guys were just assholes
killed by other assholes.

10:51.108 --> 10:52.818
Well, lookie here.

10:54.945 --> 10:56.489
Check out the building
on the hill.

10:59.909 --> 11:01.702
You've gotta be shitting me.

11:04.747 --> 11:06.748
Fuck yeah, let's go.

11:06.749 --> 11:08.209
You sure about that?

11:14.882 --> 11:16.801
Oh, my God, are you
gonna fucking tell me?

11:18.135 --> 11:20.762
If you paint a sign big enough
to be seen for miles away,

11:20.763 --> 11:22.597
that means you want people
to know that you're there,

11:22.598 --> 11:25.433
which also means
more likely than not,
you're prepared.

11:25.434 --> 11:27.186
And?

11:29.063 --> 11:31.357
They're on a hill,
so they'll see us coming.

11:32.650 --> 11:35.110
On horseback
in broad daylight, so...

11:35.111 --> 11:37.320
just a little.

11:37.321 --> 11:39.156
So, we wait until dark
and we head out on foot.

11:40.199 --> 11:41.991
And right here
is the perfect place to hole up

11:41.992 --> 11:43.993
because, well,
no one's around.

11:43.994 --> 11:47.664
Which you proved brilliantly
with your tank hatch maneuver.

11:47.665 --> 11:48.874
Dick.

11:49.959 --> 11:52.544
Alright, let's look for a door
we can fit Shimmer through.

11:52.545 --> 11:54.088
Already found that.

11:59.218 --> 12:01.220
[metal door creaking open]

12:05.182 --> 12:07.184
[Shimmer grunting]

12:15.609 --> 12:18.612
[♪ gentle music playing]

12:37.339 --> 12:40.259
♪

12:55.149 --> 12:56.399
[cymbal tings]

12:56.400 --> 12:58.401
[drum bangs]

12:58.402 --> 12:59.695
[cymbal tings]

13:02.907 --> 13:05.910
[♪ Dina begins playing drums]

13:13.083 --> 13:15.043
[Dina]
Shout if something
tries to kill you!

13:15.044 --> 13:16.170
That's the plan.

13:17.254 --> 13:19.006
[♪ drums lightly playing]

13:20.925 --> 13:23.928
[breeze blowing]

13:28.349 --> 13:31.352
[♪ gentle music playing]

13:59.421 --> 14:01.173
[sighs, kisses]

14:08.806 --> 14:10.683
[strings glissing]

14:15.896 --> 14:17.898
[guitar tuning in distance]

14:23.737 --> 14:25.739
[tuning continues]

14:41.005 --> 14:44.383
[♪ Ellie playing
"Take On Me" by A-ha]

14:57.104 --> 15:00.065
♪ Talkin' away ♪

15:01.150 --> 15:04.652
♪ I don't know what
I'm to say ♪

15:04.653 --> 15:07.698
♪ I'll say it anyway ♪

15:08.908 --> 15:13.494
♪ Today's another day
to find you ♪

15:13.495 --> 15:15.956
- ♪ Shyin'... ♪
- [floor creaking]

15:21.629 --> 15:22.838
[softly] Go on.

15:23.589 --> 15:24.590
[softly] Okay.

15:27.009 --> 15:28.844
♪ Shying away ♪

15:31.221 --> 15:34.515
♪ I'll be comin'
for your love, okay ♪

15:34.516 --> 15:39.438
♪ Take on me ♪

15:42.608 --> 15:48.322
♪ Take me on ♪

15:50.616 --> 15:56.746
♪ I'll be gone ♪

15:56.747 --> 16:00.584
♪ In a day or two ♪

16:06.090 --> 16:08.801
♪ So needless to say ♪

16:10.094 --> 16:14.138
♪ I'm odds and ends,
but I'll be ♪

16:14.139 --> 16:16.976
♪ Stumbling away ♪

16:18.185 --> 16:22.647
♪ Slowly learning
that life is okay ♪

16:22.648 --> 16:24.692
♪ Say after me ♪

16:26.694 --> 16:30.279
♪ It's no better
to be safe than sorry ♪

16:30.280 --> 16:35.577
♪ Take on me ♪

16:38.288 --> 16:43.335
♪ Take me on ♪

16:46.380 --> 16:52.760
♪ I'll be gone ♪

16:52.761 --> 16:56.098
♪ In a day or two ♪

17:00.686 --> 17:04.439
♪ In a day or two ♪

17:04.440 --> 17:06.442
[♪ guitar stops]

17:09.820 --> 17:10.988
Uh...

17:14.283 --> 17:15.993
You've gotten pretty good.

17:17.870 --> 17:20.788
Uh, thanks.

17:20.789 --> 17:22.624
All those lessons from Joel.

17:24.334 --> 17:25.669
He taught you well.

17:27.963 --> 17:29.089
He did.

17:32.760 --> 17:34.886
- You hungry?
- Starving.

17:34.887 --> 17:37.639
Great. Come on.
I'll make us beef jerky.

17:38.599 --> 17:41.268
- [both chuckle]
- Okay.

17:43.145 --> 17:45.147
[footsteps receding]

17:49.276 --> 17:51.361
- [birds chirping]
- [breeze blowing]

17:54.573 --> 17:57.034
[footsteps approaching]

17:59.953 --> 18:01.662
[gas hissing]

18:01.663 --> 18:02.831
[match striking]

18:03.665 --> 18:05.000
[flames whooshing]

18:06.376 --> 18:07.711
[blows]

18:16.095 --> 18:19.430
You know, when I was
a-- a younger man,

18:19.431 --> 18:21.766
and I wanted
to impress a woman,

18:21.767 --> 18:24.227
well, you-- you have
to know your strengths.

18:24.228 --> 18:27.355
And I was kinda shy.

18:27.356 --> 18:29.065
I-- I didn't know
how to talk to women.

18:29.066 --> 18:30.733
It made me nervous.

18:30.734 --> 18:34.696
So, what I would do
is cook for them.

18:36.448 --> 18:37.866
And I was good.

18:39.076 --> 18:40.952
Good enough
to deserve quality tools.

18:40.953 --> 18:42.537
Ah, but did I have
the money for that?

18:42.538 --> 18:43.789
No, I did not.

18:44.790 --> 18:48.126
I would go into
Williams-Sonoma.

18:48.127 --> 18:49.837
It's a cookware store.
You wouldn't know.

18:52.131 --> 18:55.759
And I would stare...

18:56.510 --> 18:57.761
at these.

18:59.179 --> 19:00.304
Mauviel.

19:00.305 --> 19:02.474
Best of the best.
French, of course.

19:04.059 --> 19:05.810
And I would think, okay,

19:05.811 --> 19:09.063
30 years to retirement
and pension, but one day,

19:09.064 --> 19:12.151
I will own a Mauviel
sauce pan...

19:14.194 --> 19:15.778
with lid.

19:15.779 --> 19:17.156
And I was right.

19:19.825 --> 19:21.451
Just not how I planned.

19:26.707 --> 19:29.209
The strange benefits
of the apocalypse.

19:33.881 --> 19:34.965
[clangs loudly]

19:35.841 --> 19:37.592
Now, copper's a bit
of a pain in the ass.

19:37.593 --> 19:38.634
You have to polish it a lot.

19:38.635 --> 19:41.262
But it heats
faster than anything.

19:41.263 --> 19:42.681
Highly conductive.

19:43.724 --> 19:45.766
Of course, this means
it doesn't retain heat

19:45.767 --> 19:48.102
the way cast iron does,
which of the two,

19:48.103 --> 19:51.106
makes copper
the inferior choice for
interrogations, but...

19:52.774 --> 19:56.486
if you own Mauviel,
you use Mauviel.

19:58.989 --> 20:00.448
She--

20:00.449 --> 20:03.034
- She watches over me.
- Then she's been watching you

20:03.035 --> 20:04.369
get your ass kicked.

20:05.370 --> 20:07.455
You know there are even
Scars who don't believe

20:07.456 --> 20:09.332
she's some magic fairy
in the sky, yeah?

20:09.333 --> 20:11.959
Some of you
actually understand
she was just a person.

20:11.960 --> 20:13.545
Heretics.

20:15.297 --> 20:16.381
Of course.

20:19.009 --> 20:21.385
The steel handles
stay cool.

20:21.386 --> 20:22.721
It's the little touches.

20:24.056 --> 20:26.058
[♪ tense music playing]

20:34.274 --> 20:36.693
Where are the Scars
attacking next?

20:37.903 --> 20:39.905
[breathing heavily]

20:41.198 --> 20:42.616
Seraphites.

20:45.494 --> 20:46.995
Hold out your hand.

20:55.921 --> 20:57.923
[breathing heavily]

20:59.383 --> 21:03.177
- [sizzling]
- [Malcolm screaming]

21:03.178 --> 21:05.513
Jesus.
This is so fucked.

21:05.514 --> 21:08.100
[WLF guard] Shut up.
Isaac knows what he's doing.

21:09.184 --> 21:11.186
[Malcolm whimpering]

21:12.771 --> 21:16.190
[Malcolm] The blood!
[sobbing]

21:16.191 --> 21:17.484
Yes, sir.

21:19.278 --> 21:21.028
- [pan clanks]
- [Malcolm] She watches over me.

21:21.029 --> 21:23.781
She fills my soul.
She watches over me.

21:23.782 --> 21:25.241
She fills my soul.

21:25.242 --> 21:27.785
She watches over me.
She fills my soul.

21:27.786 --> 21:29.954
- She watches over--
- She fills your soul.

21:29.955 --> 21:32.039
You put an arrow
in a little boy's head.

21:32.040 --> 21:34.417
Was she filling
your soul then?

21:34.418 --> 21:36.127
She tell you
to kill children?

21:36.128 --> 21:38.587
- You kill our children.
- Never by choice.

21:38.588 --> 21:40.256
You trained them
to shoot at us.

21:40.257 --> 21:41.716
Because your Wolves
kill them.

21:41.717 --> 21:43.759
Because you trained
them to shoot at us.

21:43.760 --> 21:45.428
Because you
broke the truce.

21:45.429 --> 21:46.971
- Because you broke the truce.
- Because--

21:46.972 --> 21:48.723
Because you broke it
because we broke it.

21:48.724 --> 21:50.975
I'm not playing your
little chicken-and-egg
games today, Scar.

21:50.976 --> 21:53.562
Where is the next attack?

21:53.895 --> 21:55.897
[breathing shakily]

22:01.570 --> 22:03.612
You're gonna lose.

22:03.613 --> 22:04.781
[scoffs]

22:05.449 --> 22:06.658
Are we?

22:08.869 --> 22:09.953
Son...

22:11.913 --> 22:14.290
we have automatic weapons
and hospitals,

22:14.291 --> 22:18.002
and you lunatics
have bolt-action rifles,

22:18.003 --> 22:20.047
bows and arrows,
and superstition.

22:21.840 --> 22:24.801
So, tell me,
how are we going to lose?

22:26.928 --> 22:28.138
[sighs]

22:31.725 --> 22:34.602
[voice shaking]
Every day,
one of your Wolves

22:34.603 --> 22:36.854
comes to see the truth,

22:36.855 --> 22:38.647
and takes Her
into their heart.

22:38.648 --> 22:42.610
Every day.
Every day, a Wolf leaves you

22:42.611 --> 22:46.614
to take the holy mortification
to become a Seraphite.

22:46.615 --> 22:50.619
And none of us ever leave...

22:51.703 --> 22:53.246
to become a Wolf.

22:57.042 --> 22:59.460
I will burn every part of you

22:59.461 --> 23:01.797
until you tell me
what I want to know!

23:03.006 --> 23:05.008
[labored breathing]

23:06.176 --> 23:08.261
[♪ tense music continues]

23:13.308 --> 23:15.142
[pan clangs]

23:15.143 --> 23:16.727
- [gunshot]
- [bullet shell clinking]

23:16.728 --> 23:19.523
- [body thuds]
- [WLF guard] Good.

23:24.403 --> 23:26.279
Scar got what he deserved.

23:30.200 --> 23:31.618
Fucking animal.

23:33.328 --> 23:35.330
[thunder rumbling]

23:36.456 --> 23:37.707
No patrol.

23:39.000 --> 23:41.211
- That's a good sign.
- Not always.

23:42.921 --> 23:45.506
So, the front entrance
is like a security door.

23:45.507 --> 23:47.425
There's a camera
right over it,
which means we go

23:47.426 --> 23:48.885
around the back.

23:50.887 --> 23:52.013
Window.

23:54.808 --> 23:56.977
Oh, boy.

23:59.020 --> 24:00.397
Second floor.

24:05.694 --> 24:06.861
[thunder booms]

24:06.862 --> 24:08.863
[Ellie] So, somebody
hopped onto the shed,

24:08.864 --> 24:10.698
climbed the downspout,
broke the window,

24:10.699 --> 24:12.242
and got cut on the way in?

24:13.618 --> 24:15.620
Well, I guess
that's our way in, too.

24:16.788 --> 24:19.749
And if we run into Wolves
that weren't in Jackson?

24:27.674 --> 24:28.717
Agreed.

24:29.718 --> 24:31.720
[metal banging]

24:33.680 --> 24:35.140
[Ellie grunting]

24:42.564 --> 24:44.441
[whispering]
You can do that.
You're good.

24:48.653 --> 24:51.656
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

25:00.624 --> 25:01.833
[door handle clicking]

25:08.673 --> 25:11.426
[Ellie]
What the fuck is this?

25:13.136 --> 25:15.138
[thunder rumbling]

25:18.850 --> 25:21.102
- He isn't one of them.
- [Dina] No.

25:23.605 --> 25:26.024
But we're definitely
in the right place.

25:30.237 --> 25:33.240
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

25:44.876 --> 25:46.878
[door handle clacking]

25:48.004 --> 25:50.006
[metal door creaking loudly]

25:57.305 --> 26:00.808
[♪ dramatic music playing]

26:00.809 --> 26:03.352
[thunder rumbling]

26:03.353 --> 26:05.397
[ropes creaking]

26:06.731 --> 26:07.732
[Ellie gasps]

26:09.484 --> 26:10.901
- [Dina retching]
- Dina?

26:10.902 --> 26:12.779
[retching]
Ellie, g-- go.

26:13.780 --> 26:15.782
[retching continues]

26:20.745 --> 26:22.664
[Ellie] These aren't
any of them either.

26:27.919 --> 26:30.922
- [ropes creaking]
- [thunder rumbling]

26:53.570 --> 26:56.323
That group we saw
in the woods,
they did this.

26:57.240 --> 26:59.159
What the fuck is wrong
with Seattle?

27:01.494 --> 27:03.496
[radio static]

27:11.087 --> 27:12.088
[Dina grunts]

27:14.049 --> 27:16.216
It's the same ones we use.

27:16.217 --> 27:18.552
- If she called for backup--
- Yeah, we gotta get outta here.

27:18.553 --> 27:20.847
- [people chattering in distance]
- Shit, get down. Down!

27:22.932 --> 27:24.684
[banging]

27:26.686 --> 27:27.937
[soldier]
Oh, my God.

27:30.607 --> 27:31.816
Fuck me.

27:33.610 --> 27:35.736
- Look at this.
- Who the fuck would do that?

27:35.737 --> 27:37.738
Scars got all of 'em.

27:37.739 --> 27:39.573
I don't see
Brancaccio or Welsh,

27:39.574 --> 27:41.618
but, yeah,
it's the rest of 'em.

27:42.994 --> 27:44.578
[commander]
You, cut 'em down.

27:44.579 --> 27:46.246
[soldier]
Shouldn't we secure
the station first?

27:46.247 --> 27:48.290
[commander]
I said cut them
the fuck down.

27:48.291 --> 27:51.168
The rest of you, fan out.
And go slow.

27:51.169 --> 27:53.962
If the Scars are still here,
find them and kill them.

27:53.963 --> 27:55.756
[soldier 2]
Isaac said he wants 'em
alive for questioning.

27:55.757 --> 27:57.341
[commander]
Isaac's not here, okay?

27:57.342 --> 27:59.093
With intestines all
over the fuckin' place.

27:59.094 --> 28:00.636
So, I don't really
give a shit.

28:00.637 --> 28:03.013
I don't give a shit
if it's a woman or a kid.

28:03.014 --> 28:04.473
I don't care
if it's a fuckin' baby.

28:04.474 --> 28:07.519
Look what they did.
Now, fan the fuck out!

28:15.402 --> 28:16.695
[soldier 1] Clear!

28:19.989 --> 28:22.992
[♪ tense music playing]

28:25.870 --> 28:27.163
[soldier 2]
This side's clear.

28:32.585 --> 28:33.837
[soldier 3] Clear.

28:38.800 --> 28:41.803
[♪ tense music
continues playing]

28:44.139 --> 28:45.140
[soldier 4] Clear!

28:51.896 --> 28:53.481
[distant clacking]

28:57.902 --> 28:58.987
[soldier] Clear.

29:02.198 --> 29:03.491
Stairs clear.

29:07.871 --> 29:10.874
[♪ tense music continues]

29:14.210 --> 29:16.212
[thunder rumbling]

29:17.213 --> 29:19.799
- [grunting softly]
- [clattering in distance]

29:25.263 --> 29:27.265
[labored breathing]

29:42.322 --> 29:44.407
[grunting]

29:49.329 --> 29:50.538
[soldier grunting]

29:54.918 --> 29:56.002
[soldier] We got one!

30:00.048 --> 30:02.049
- [gunshot]
- [body thuds]

30:02.050 --> 30:03.217
Shoot that window!

30:03.218 --> 30:04.551
[soldiers shouting]

30:04.552 --> 30:06.220
[soldier]
Move, move, move, move!

30:06.221 --> 30:08.263
- [gunfire]
- [glass shattering]

30:08.264 --> 30:09.557
Go!

30:12.685 --> 30:14.020
[Dina] Come on!

30:15.855 --> 30:17.857
[thunder crashing]

30:21.736 --> 30:22.903
[grunting]

30:22.904 --> 30:24.614
Come on. Get up!

30:26.699 --> 30:28.242
[soldiers shouting]

30:28.243 --> 30:29.661
[gunfire]

30:33.373 --> 30:34.541
[thunder crashing]

30:37.544 --> 30:39.546
[soldiers shouting in distance]

30:41.089 --> 30:43.298
- Fuck!
- Shit!

30:43.299 --> 30:44.759
[Ellie] This way!

30:48.304 --> 30:50.306
- [Dina] Aw, shit!
- [Ellie] Fuck!

30:52.225 --> 30:54.101
[soldier]
We see them!
We see them!

30:54.102 --> 30:55.853
Go. We can fit,
they can't.

30:55.854 --> 30:57.480
Come on, come on,
come on, come on.

30:59.148 --> 31:00.149
[Ellie grunting]

31:01.192 --> 31:03.194
- [gunfire]
- [bullets ricocheting]

31:10.159 --> 31:13.246
They're in the transit tunnel.
Circle the south entrance.

31:15.748 --> 31:17.750
[water dripping]

31:22.213 --> 31:24.215
[rustling]

31:34.726 --> 31:36.144
[grunting]

31:55.663 --> 31:58.582
[rocks clattering]

31:58.583 --> 32:01.168
- [Dina grunting]
- [Ellie] [sighs] Okay.

32:01.169 --> 32:03.545
- [Dina panting]
- You good?

32:03.546 --> 32:04.756
Yeah.

32:07.216 --> 32:09.509
Is this place gonna
fall down on us?

32:09.510 --> 32:11.219
I'd rather not find out.

32:11.220 --> 32:12.889
Let's go.
That way.

32:13.806 --> 32:15.391
[loud bang echoing]

32:21.814 --> 32:24.817
[♪ ominous music playing]

32:29.072 --> 32:30.782
[flare striking]

32:46.255 --> 32:48.007
[footsteps crunching]

32:59.519 --> 33:01.521
[distant screeching]

33:06.317 --> 33:08.319
[distant clicking]

33:12.991 --> 33:14.993
[distant screeching continues]

33:19.455 --> 33:21.708
[whispering]
I thought it was
supposed to be empty.

33:24.627 --> 33:25.920
[whispering]
Yeah. It was.

33:27.922 --> 33:29.674
[screeching continues]

33:31.926 --> 33:33.928
[clicking, screeching
intensifying]

33:41.227 --> 33:43.980
[screeching, clicking
continue]

33:58.036 --> 34:00.038
[screeching intensifies]

34:01.414 --> 34:04.083
- [gunfire]
- [soldiers screaming]

34:06.961 --> 34:08.963
[infected horde screeching]

34:11.924 --> 34:12.925
This way!

34:14.510 --> 34:16.262
- [infected snarling]
- Dina!

34:19.015 --> 34:20.891
[gunfire continues]

34:20.892 --> 34:22.268
- [soldiers shouting]
- [Dina] Ellie, fast!

34:25.313 --> 34:28.107
[both grunting]

34:29.567 --> 34:30.860
Shit!

34:32.361 --> 34:35.030
- [infected screeching]
- [loud banging]

34:35.031 --> 34:36.324
Go! Go!

34:40.078 --> 34:41.870
[infected yelling]

34:41.871 --> 34:43.705
Oh, my God!
Go, go, go!

34:43.706 --> 34:45.750
[Ellie and Dina grunting]

34:48.044 --> 34:50.670
[loud banging]

34:50.671 --> 34:52.715
[infected screeching]

34:54.008 --> 34:55.885
[Dina gasping]

35:01.224 --> 35:03.934
[screeching]

35:03.935 --> 35:05.978
[loud banging continues]

35:08.523 --> 35:10.440
[glass shattering]

35:10.441 --> 35:11.858
[Ellie exclaiming]

35:11.859 --> 35:13.402
[gunshots]

35:18.616 --> 35:20.575
- Fuck!
- Get it!

35:20.576 --> 35:22.245
[glass shattering]

35:23.830 --> 35:26.289
[gunshots]

35:26.290 --> 35:27.582
Ellie!

35:27.583 --> 35:29.252
Up!

35:29.961 --> 35:32.379
- [gunshots continue]
- [Dina grunting]

35:32.380 --> 35:33.422
Shit!

35:34.257 --> 35:36.466
- [glass shattering]
- [infected screeching]

35:36.467 --> 35:37.510
Ellie!

35:39.887 --> 35:43.431
- [grunting]
- [Dina exclaiming]

35:43.432 --> 35:44.892
- [glass shatters]
- [Ellie yells]

35:50.398 --> 35:51.399
Jump!

35:52.400 --> 35:54.360
[infected snarling]

35:57.905 --> 35:59.907
[loud banging]

36:00.908 --> 36:02.242
The fence!

36:02.243 --> 36:04.245
[both panting]

36:09.083 --> 36:10.626
[screeching]

36:16.632 --> 36:17.799
[fence rattling]

36:17.800 --> 36:18.926
[grunting]

36:36.569 --> 36:38.361
[grunting]

36:38.362 --> 36:40.198
Fucking open!

36:45.119 --> 36:46.203
Fucking move!

36:46.204 --> 36:47.955
[panting]

36:53.002 --> 36:54.628
[screeching]

36:54.629 --> 36:56.713
[Ellie shouting]

36:56.714 --> 36:57.924
[screaming]

37:01.886 --> 37:03.221
[gunshot]

37:04.305 --> 37:05.640
[metal squeaking]

37:07.225 --> 37:09.227
[♪ dramatic music playing]

37:10.228 --> 37:12.146
[both grunting]

37:18.194 --> 37:19.779
[bodies crunching]

37:22.031 --> 37:23.491
Dina.

37:24.158 --> 37:26.160
Come on!
[grunting]

37:28.079 --> 37:29.205
Dina, come on!

37:33.209 --> 37:35.211
[thunder rumbling]

37:39.090 --> 37:40.258
Maybe there.

37:44.512 --> 37:46.555
Come on, we've gotta
get outta sight!

37:52.103 --> 37:54.105
- [water dripping]
- [thunder continues rumbling]

38:10.705 --> 38:12.205
[Ellie]
We can hole up here for now.

38:12.206 --> 38:13.916
I'll bar the door.

38:17.253 --> 38:19.255
[thunder crashing]

38:29.890 --> 38:32.058
Okay, it's not perfect,
but if anyone tries to get in,

38:32.059 --> 38:33.477
it'll buy us some ti...

38:37.148 --> 38:39.275
The fuck are you doing?

38:40.192 --> 38:42.320
[panicked breathing]

38:47.825 --> 38:48.826
[softly] Okay.

38:51.078 --> 38:54.122
Okay. Okay,
I know you're scared.

38:54.123 --> 38:56.666
- Please, don't.
- But I need you to
understand something.

38:56.667 --> 38:58.626
[Dina]
Please don't make this
any harder than it has to be.

38:58.627 --> 39:00.253
- Wait.
- Why did you do that?

39:00.254 --> 39:01.963
Why the fuck did you
have to do that?

39:01.964 --> 39:03.423
Please listen to me.

39:03.424 --> 39:05.342
I would die for you.
I would.

39:05.343 --> 39:07.053
But that is not
what just happened.

39:11.849 --> 39:13.392
Fuck. I'm immune.

39:14.143 --> 39:15.519
I can't get infected.

39:16.604 --> 39:19.106
[Dina crying]

39:20.649 --> 39:22.443
Dina, do not
fucking shoot me!

39:23.402 --> 39:25.905
I've been bitten before.
I'm still here.

39:27.990 --> 39:30.450
I don't-- I know you
don't believe me.

39:30.451 --> 39:33.037
I get it, I wouldn't
believe me either, but...

39:35.331 --> 39:37.040
Here's what we're gonna do.

39:37.041 --> 39:39.793
I'm gonna walk over there
nice and slow,

39:39.794 --> 39:41.628
to that big fucking chair,
and I'm gonna bandage my arm

39:41.629 --> 39:43.004
and I'm gonna go to sleep.

39:43.005 --> 39:45.298
You're gonna sit
as far away from me
as you want,

39:45.299 --> 39:47.300
and you're gonna keep
that gun pointed on me.

39:47.301 --> 39:49.010
If I turn, shoot me.

39:49.011 --> 39:51.846
But I promise.
[sighs]

39:51.847 --> 39:53.891
A lot of the times,
I wish this wasn't true...

39:54.225 --> 39:56.227
[thunder rumbling]

39:57.561 --> 40:00.064
...I'm gonna wake up
exactly as I am right now.

40:03.109 --> 40:04.401
Me.

40:04.402 --> 40:06.487
[Dina panting]

40:10.533 --> 40:11.534
[softly] Okay.

40:14.120 --> 40:15.871
[sighs deeply]

40:20.042 --> 40:22.044
[thunder continues rumbling]

40:25.047 --> 40:27.049
[breathing heavily]

40:32.346 --> 40:34.681
[water dripping]

40:34.682 --> 40:36.725
[thunder rumbling]

40:38.894 --> 40:39.895
[water drop plunks]

40:44.733 --> 40:45.985
[groaning]

40:48.195 --> 40:49.362
Uh, it's just water!

40:49.363 --> 40:50.656
Rain fell on my face,
that's all.

40:52.199 --> 40:54.201
[Ellie panting]

41:00.249 --> 41:03.377
See?
No shaking.

41:06.922 --> 41:08.549
I'm gonna stand up now.

41:17.600 --> 41:19.602
[panting]

41:22.897 --> 41:24.565
Can I show you?

41:33.991 --> 41:35.993
[breathing heavily]

41:39.663 --> 41:43.292
[♪ dramatic music playing]

41:59.433 --> 42:01.060
[thunder rumbling]

42:01.435 --> 42:02.478
[flashlight clicks]

42:12.446 --> 42:14.448
[breathing shakily]

42:26.126 --> 42:28.128
[thunder crashing]

42:39.098 --> 42:40.683
[voice breaking]
Ellie.

42:41.642 --> 42:42.643
Yeah?

42:43.811 --> 42:46.397
[both breathing shakily]

42:48.983 --> 42:50.401
I'm pregnant.

42:54.947 --> 42:56.240
What?

42:58.659 --> 43:01.662
[♪ soft music playing]

43:15.926 --> 43:17.928
[both breathing heavily]

43:30.941 --> 43:32.943
[Dina moaning]

43:39.575 --> 43:42.578
[♪ soft music continues playing]

43:54.798 --> 43:55.799
[kisses]

44:00.512 --> 44:01.764
[Dina groans softly]

44:06.810 --> 44:07.977
Wait, no!

44:07.978 --> 44:10.480
No.
Morning breath.

44:10.481 --> 44:13.025
- [groaning]
- It's gross. Hold on.

44:22.117 --> 44:24.119
[backpack unzipping]

44:26.288 --> 44:28.331
I don't know if this
is gonna be better.

44:28.332 --> 44:29.625
[Dina]
It'll be better.

44:37.341 --> 44:39.425
Mm. Beefy.

44:39.426 --> 44:40.803
[both chuckle]

44:41.929 --> 44:43.429
Mm.
[blows, sniffs]

44:43.430 --> 44:44.682
Mm!

44:58.195 --> 44:59.488
How's it doing?

45:02.116 --> 45:03.534
Wow, that's...

45:11.792 --> 45:13.961
Is this where you
were bitten before?

45:14.753 --> 45:15.754
Yep.

45:17.381 --> 45:20.300
- You said it was a burn.
- Most of it is.

45:24.179 --> 45:25.723
You did it to yourself?

45:28.559 --> 45:30.936
[whispering]
I really wanted to wear
short sleeves again.

45:32.730 --> 45:35.398
[Dina chuckles]

45:35.399 --> 45:36.691
It's a little thing,
but when you start

45:36.692 --> 45:38.526
to hide little things,
they become big things.

45:38.527 --> 45:39.862
You don't say.

45:49.580 --> 45:50.748
Why now?

45:59.131 --> 46:00.883
I thought you were gone.

46:04.094 --> 46:06.345
And then all of a sudden,

46:06.346 --> 46:08.098
this future
I was imagining...

46:10.184 --> 46:11.518
wasn't gonna happen.

46:14.438 --> 46:18.525
Where we're together,
and we have a kid, and...

46:20.611 --> 46:22.362
I don't even know
if you want that.

46:25.282 --> 46:26.867
I want it with you.

46:31.246 --> 46:33.540
I'm sorry it took so long.

46:35.250 --> 46:36.835
I knew how
you felt about me.

46:37.836 --> 46:40.963
How?
I was hiding it really well.

46:40.964 --> 46:43.299
No, you kind of
fucking weren't.

46:43.300 --> 46:45.426
- Oh.
- I'm sorry.

46:45.427 --> 46:47.595
I wanted to.

46:47.596 --> 46:48.722
Yeah?

46:52.810 --> 46:54.353
When I was little...

46:56.480 --> 46:59.774
I told my mother I liked boys
and I liked girls.

46:59.775 --> 47:03.069
And she said,
"No, you like boys."

47:03.070 --> 47:04.112
[Ellie] Hm.

47:05.239 --> 47:06.615
And it just...

47:09.576 --> 47:12.496
I got stuck.

47:14.414 --> 47:16.083
Even after she died, it...

47:18.877 --> 47:21.004
I tried to make things
work with Jesse

47:21.922 --> 47:24.758
because I like him.
I do, I think
he's a really good guy.

47:26.218 --> 47:28.512
But he wasn't the one.

47:31.682 --> 47:33.100
Still kept trying anyway.

47:34.893 --> 47:38.522
Couldn't let myself just...
be.

47:41.900 --> 47:43.861
You were scared.

47:45.904 --> 47:48.197
Not everyone's
as brave as you.

47:48.198 --> 47:50.950
I'm not brave.
I'm just obvious.

47:50.951 --> 47:53.494
[Dina laughing]

47:53.495 --> 47:54.996
Shut up!

47:54.997 --> 47:57.039
[both giggle]

47:57.040 --> 47:59.793
[♪ soft music playing]

48:13.765 --> 48:15.267
[Dina chuckles]

48:17.978 --> 48:20.105
How do you know
for sure that you're...

48:21.023 --> 48:23.983
Oh!
I started wondering

48:23.984 --> 48:26.527
after we saw the bodies
in the forest,

48:26.528 --> 48:29.030
because I've seen
fucked-up shit before
without barfing.

48:29.031 --> 48:32.033
And I knew morning sickness
was a thing,

48:32.034 --> 48:34.577
and I was late, which I--
I've never been regular,

48:34.578 --> 48:36.829
but I was very late.

48:36.830 --> 48:39.582
And then, I found
a pregnancy test

48:39.583 --> 48:42.668
at the pharmacy,
and I peed on it.

48:42.669 --> 48:45.004
- You pee on it?
- That's how it works.

48:45.005 --> 48:46.672
I don't just randomly
piss on stuff.

48:46.673 --> 48:48.257
Oh, okay.
That's good.

48:48.258 --> 48:49.301
Here.

48:50.469 --> 48:51.887
Two lines means pregnant.

48:54.097 --> 48:55.765
This thing's pretty old.

48:55.766 --> 48:57.100
- How do you--
- And here.

48:58.477 --> 49:00.270
And here's a couple more.

49:08.987 --> 49:11.782
So, we're having a baby.

49:13.533 --> 49:16.161
I mean, we, and also
I guess Jesse are--

49:16.995 --> 49:18.413
It was Jesse, right?

49:21.291 --> 49:24.086
- [scoffs lightly]
- So, we're all having a baby.

49:25.796 --> 49:26.964
Holy shit.

49:30.717 --> 49:33.929
- I'm gonna be a dad.
- [chuckles] Yeah.

49:34.972 --> 49:36.806
- [booming in distance]
- [both gasp]

49:36.807 --> 49:38.641
[booming continues]

49:38.642 --> 49:40.226
[solider] [on radio]
...south of Pike.
Heavy fire.

49:40.227 --> 49:42.061
Scars broke through
the north side of the FOB.

49:42.062 --> 49:44.063
- [medical] Casualties?
- [soldier] At least two dozen.

49:44.064 --> 49:46.942
We're falling back.
Bringing wounded to Lakehill.

49:47.859 --> 49:49.735
- Tell Nora to get ready.
- [gunfire over radio]

49:49.736 --> 49:51.237
Oh, fuck!

49:51.238 --> 49:53.281
[radio static]

49:55.492 --> 49:57.243
- He just said Nora.
- Yeah.

49:57.244 --> 49:59.328
- She's gonna know--
- Where Abby is, yeah.

49:59.329 --> 50:00.579
That's Lakehill

50:00.580 --> 50:02.832
but I don't know
where we are anymore.

50:02.833 --> 50:05.002
Okay, we go up high
and we look around.
Come on.

50:08.171 --> 50:11.174
[♪ dramatic music playing]

50:14.386 --> 50:17.389
[explosions, gunfire
in distance]

50:34.072 --> 50:35.157
Ellie.

50:36.491 --> 50:38.784
See that white building
out there?

50:38.785 --> 50:41.538
That's it.
That's Lakehill.

50:43.081 --> 50:45.083
[distant gunfire continues]

50:55.135 --> 50:57.970
You don't have to go.
You can stay here.

50:57.971 --> 50:59.722
- Fuck you.
- No, I'm not saying...

50:59.723 --> 51:01.807
[distant explosions continue]

51:01.808 --> 51:04.185
